.SH "BUGS"
This script imports \fBssrepi\fR rather than \fBrecord\fR, unlike most other scripts in the RECORD suite (with the exception of \fBrecord\-image\-provenance\.py\fR, which has the same inconsistency)\. It is unclear whether this is intentional (the script predates the renaming of the library from SSREPI to RECORD) or an oversight\.
.P
The output path \fBservices\.dot\fR, the entity types, and the label fields are all hard\-coded and cannot be changed without editing the script\.
.P
Any existing \fBservices\.dot\fR in the current working directory is silently overwritten\.
.P
The \fB__credits__\fR field is empty\.
.P
The graph as configured contains no edges between \fBApplications\fR, \fBComputers\fR, and \fBSpecifications\fR unless \fBssrepi\.draw_graph\fR derives relationships automatically from foreign keys; the script itself supplies no explicit relationship information\.
.P
The word "services" in the module comment is misspelled as "serivces"\.
